import asm65816

// Warp Styles DX
// Expanded warp styles table and support for colourful fades
// SupremeKirb

/*
== Adding new warp styles ==
Add a warp style by adding a new WarpStyle to the end of
ExpandedWarpStyles below.
The format is:
    duration: duration in frames (255 max)
    swirl: swirl to play during the transition
    swirl flags: flags for the swirl
    fade: fade multiplier. =< 50 for a fade to black, > 50 for a fade to white
    direction: direction to slide the screen in
    colour: entry in the fade colour table (we'll come to this)
    slide speed: angle/speed to slide the screen at (such as in moonside)
    start sfx: sound effect to play at the start of the warp
    second duration: duration when fading back in
    second swirl: swirl to play when fading back in
    second swirl flags: flags for the swirl when fading back in
    second sfx: sound effect to play when fading back in

Please note: slide speed has been made less precise as a result of
the colour field. Now, only the high byte is used. This only affects
two vanilla warps, which have been rounded up from 0x07E8 to 0x0800.
*/

/*
== About coloured fades ==
In the colour field, you can put an index into the FadeColourTable.
If the colour field is zero, it will use the fade multiplier to
perform a black or white fade as is the vanilla behaviour.

Otherwise, it will fade to and from the colour in that index in
the FadeColourTable. The colour format is the SNES's BGR555 format.

To convert from hex/HTML to BGR555:
Take the five most significant bits of each colour
Place them in the order B-G-R with a leading zero bit
For example: #AABBCC 
R: AA --> 10101|010 (look at five most significant)
G: BB --> 10111|011
B: CC --> 11001|100
Becomes...
Z BLUE  GREEN RED
0|11001|10111|10101
= 0x66F5

Or use this Python to convert:
```
def BGR555(input: int):
    r = ((input & 0xFF0000) >> 16) >> 3
    g = ((input & 0x00FF00) >> 8) >> 3
    b = (input & 0x0000FF) >> 3
    return hex((b << 10) | (g << 5) | r)
```

*/

FadeColourTable: {
    // 0 (dummy index)
    FadeColour(0x0000)
    // 1
    FadeColour(0x5D70) // magic butterfly lavender
    // 2
    // add your own!
}

